# Resource governance (guiding principle)

This system exists to **achieve goals while managing scarce resources**. Time is rarely the bottleneck; **resource discipline** is.

Optimize in this order when making tradeoffs:

## 1. Search tokens

Spend search/browse budget only when local knowledge is insufficient.

- **Code first:** grep, semantic search, read known paths, ledger, `AGENTS.md` — before web search or browser.
- **Cache wins:** reuse RSS/Intel caches, prior reports, MemPalace records; do not re-fetch what the repo already holds.
- **Heavy browse last:** Firecrawl / browser automation on linuxbox (~2 GB RAM) only when a task truly needs live pages.
- **One pass:** formulate the query once; avoid search loops that restate the same question.

## 2. Memory

Right-sized recall beats transcript replay.

- **Authority:** MemPalace = durable truth; claude-mem = working cache for *this* thread. Sync on chat/agent/milestone boundaries; MemPalace wins on conflict.
- **Coordination:** `AI_GROUPCHAT.md` + git for multi-agent intent — pull before work, append `[PC]`/`[LAPTOP]`/`[LINUX]` lines.
- **Resume:** use the **`rewind`** skill (`.cursor/skills/rewind/`) to reconstruct context from artifacts, not from re-reading entire chats.
- **Promote or trim:** promote what stays true; drop stale cache and redundant copies.

## 3. Free vs paid models

Match model cost to lane criticality.

- **High-frequency / low-stakes:** free models only (`qwen/...-instruct:free` on linuxbox **fast** lane). Never point 30s crons at paid models without human sign-off.
- **Think / meta / implementation:** paid or stronger models when correctness or reasoning depth matters; prefer cheap fallbacks (`deepseek-v4-flash`) before premium.
- **Budget-aware:** OpenRouter cap is small — log model choice when starting costly work; batch LLM work; prefer deterministic scripts where possible.
- **Cloud agents (cursor.com/agents):** treat as paid capacity; use for parallel/away work, not duplicate of local lanes unless intentional.

## 4. Correctness / accuracy

Never trade away verification for speed or minimal tokens.

- **Evidence:** do not claim network, deploy, or test state without terminal output on the **right machine**.
- **Verify each step:** one concrete check per task (pytest, curl, Playwright smoke, supply-chain `SAFE` before upgrade).
- **Safety never "lazy":** validation at trust boundaries, data-loss guards, security, accessibility — see **ponytail** rule (correctness is not optional).
- **Supply-chain gate:** upgrade packages/frameworks only after `safe-update-check.sh` returns **SAFE** (auto-upgrade-if-SAFE policy).

## How the pieces fit

| Concern | Primary levers |
|---------|----------------|
| Search tokens | local tools → ledger/docs → cached intel → web/browser |
| Memory | MemPalace, claude-mem, `AI_GROUPCHAT.md`, `rewind` skill |
| Model spend | Hermes profiles (fast/think/meta), lane routing, free-first crons |
| Correctness | verify loops, ponytail ladder, Karpathy guidelines, update gate |

When goals conflict: **correctness > memory hygiene > model spend > search tokens** — but prefer solutions that improve all four (e.g. a small script replaces repeated paid LLM calls).
